WEBVTT

1
00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:34.700
You think this is cute, don't you?

2
00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:38.009
You think there's a real connection there.

3
00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:40.726
So you feed it,

4
00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:42.848
you dress it up.

5
00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:48.570
But a cat doesn't care if you live or die

6
00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:51.450
as long as someone
gives it Friskies twice a day.

7
00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:04.970
But people are so desperate
for someone to hold onto

8
00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:06.929
they'll take whatever they can get.

9
00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:10.405
I found him on the street,
months after the accident

10
00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:12.528
and I dress him like Masao.

11
00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:16.161
I know my son has come back
to me in this cat.

12
00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:19.802
But no matter how lonely you are,

13
00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:23.168
a cat is not a person.

14
00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:47.846
Okay. Super helpful, uh...

15
00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:51.043
Oh, so marketing wants
sign-off on the new billboard.

16
00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:53.405
What do you think?

17
00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:55.369
It might be a little
heavy on the Photoshop.

18
00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:56.487
Get me a real F-16.

19
00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:57.607
We'll take some real pictures.

20
00:01:57.720 --> 00:01:59.449
No, they said they don't
have the budget for it.

21
00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:00.885
Fire the marketing department!

22
00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:03.247
You wanna fire the entire
marketing department?

23
00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:06.290
No. I wanna fly a real F-16. What's next?

24
00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:08.010
I'm supposed to remind you,

25
00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:09.320
Lara's left two messages.

26
00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:10.885
Why is she calling?

27
00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:12.485
Because she's your wife.

28
00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:14.927
I put together some talking points

29
00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.331
for your press conference.

30
00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:17.686
How old are you again?

31
00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:18.807
Twenty-eight.

32
00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:19.927
That's how long I've been
talking to the press.

33
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:21.001
I'll be fine.

34
00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:22.127
Sir, we're ready.

35
00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:25.684
Why don't you jump with me today?

36
00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:28.206
Oh, yeah, no. I just had breakfast, so...

37
00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:29.401
Come on!

38
00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:31.683
Dad, I can't. I can't.

39
00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:33.691
All right.

40
00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:37.563
Chicken!

41
00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:43.165
Good one, Dad.

42
00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:02.281
Yeah!

43
00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:03.771
Very nice, very nice!

44
00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:06.451
Perfect landing.

45
00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:07.851
Thank you.

46
00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:10.605
Thank you very much. Thank you.

47
00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:12.120
Good morning, everyone.

48
00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:13.361
What an incredible view.

49
00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:16.330
And I mean all of you that I get
to look at this fine morning.

50
00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:17.686
Thank you for coming.

51
00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:19.404
Now, when we open this building

52
00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:20.891
one month from today.

53
00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:23.924
The FireBrand Tower will be the tallest
building in North America.

54
00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:26.361
And that means that we can
finally move out of that dump

55
00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:28.602
we've all been forced to work in
all these years down the block.

56
00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:29.841
Tell us about Chicago.

57
00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:32.366
Mr. Brand, any comment
on the Paragon Tower?

58
00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:34.568
Oh, you mean that tin shack
they're gluing together

59
00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:35.766
over there in Chicago?

60
00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:36.887
No. No comment on that.

61
00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:39.008
Rumor is they're beating you by 60 feet.

62
00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:41.164
Well, no. There's not a chance of that.

63
00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:43.089
No, no. Look, I'd love to
answer more questions,

64
00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:44.645
but I gotta get back to the office.

65
00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:49.284
All right. I wanna move fast here.

66
00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:51.044
Have legal review this overnight.

67
00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:52.844
They're all tied up with the tower.

68
00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.570
Listen, I know we got to keep him happy,

69
00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:56.563
but we can't let this building
distract us from...

70
00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:58.244
Why? You've got something better to do?

71
00:03:58.600 --> 00:03:59.601
Oh.

72
00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:00.920
How was the press conference?

73
00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:02.889
Well, apparently it was a distraction.

74
00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:05.531
I pulled some staff to explore
a public offering.

75
00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:08.041
I'm sorry.
Did I ask you to sell my company?

76
00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:09.241
Are we taking bids?

77
00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:10.401
How much can we get for Gary?

78
00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:12.841
We ran some rough numbers...

79
00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:15.122
Yeah. Well, first, why is the press
asking me about Chicago?

80
00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:16.929
You're winning. Yours is bigger.

81
00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:19.520
Well, finally there's our new slogan.

82
00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:21.125
Where are we with the opening ceremony?

83
00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:23.123
We're gonna rig the entire
building with fireworks.

84
00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:25.209
Oh, so, wait. When I cut the ribbon...

85
00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:26.281
Fireworks go off.

86
00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:28.488
Oh, my God. Ian, that is just spectacular,

87
00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:31.040
you know, if we were doing
a Fourth of July celebration

88
00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:32.565
or a really rousing Oktoberfest.

89
00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:33.721
Tom, we can't keep...

90
00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:35.370
Look, we are just about to cap off

91
00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:37.283
the tallest building
in the Northern Hemisphere

92
00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:39.681
and I can't brag about it
if I don't own it.

93
00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:40.841
Yeah.

94
00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:43.207
This is the distraction.

95
00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:48.326
Okay, everybody,
let's pretend that that didn't just happen.

96
00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:05.200
- What's that?
- It's a surprise.

97
00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:06.281
For my birthday?

98
00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:09.289
- What are you watching?
- Dad.

99
00:05:09.960 --> 00:05:11.644
Did he tell you to record this?

100
00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:13.325
No, but I just wanted to see him.

101
00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:14.526
Look. Watch.

102
00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:16.927
And that means that we can
finally move out of that dump

103
00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:18.331
we've all been forced to work in

104
00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:19.925
all these years down the block.

105
00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:22.090
How many times have you watched this?

106
00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:23.367
Um...

107
00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:24.441
Eighty-three.

108
00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:26.291
And now it's 84.

109
00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:27.965
We're worried about costs.

110
00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:30.361
Well, that's why we call this
a "Board meeting."

111
00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:33.646
Please take a message.

112
00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:35.722
- Tom, these are serious concerns.
- I know.

113
00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:37.325
- Look, I understand...
- Lara Brand.

114
00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:41.851
- Lara Brand.
- Oh, no, go ahead. Just take it outside.

115
00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:47.248
Ian, where's Tom?
I can't get ahold of him.

116
00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:48.970
I can't pry him away from the Board.

117
00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:52.931
I wanna show you all that I take
your concerns very seriously.

118
00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:55.691
Our operating costs
are up 30% from last quarter.

119
00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:59.970
And my first concern is why is Ian
coming at us with this IPO crap?

120
00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:01.320
He's been with the Board all day?

121
00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:02.606
It's hard to get Tom's attention.

122
00:06:02.680 --> 00:06:03.886
Maybe I should join the Board.

123
00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:06.361
Or you can take my job. Please.

124
00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:08.204
Ian approached us with the idea.

125
00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:10.487
He's put together
a very attractive proposal.

126
00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:13.120
A public offering means
a big payday for all of us.

127
00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:16.124
Now, we've sunk years of revenue
into that building, Tom.

128
00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:17.486
It's time to cash out.

129
00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:19.927
Come on, we got plenty of cash, don't we?

130
00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:21.001
And why?

131
00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:23.970
Because we built airlines and retail
chains and phone companies,

132
00:06:24.040 --> 00:06:26.168
but no one is gonna remember any of those

133
00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:27.651
because they keep changing hands.

134
00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:29.404
But 100 years from now,

135
00:06:29.480 --> 00:06:31.960
when people look out their windows
and they see that tower,

136
00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:33.883
they're gonna see the name "Brand"

137
00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:35.769
and that's a name they will never forget.

138
00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:39.128
And that is not something
that I am willing to sell.

139
00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:41.328
We're not running a charity
for your ego, Tom.

140
00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:43.642
Okay. Well, then instead,
let's play a little game.

141
00:06:43.720 --> 00:06:45.324
You know, just for the fun of it.

142
00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:49.161
Raise your hand if your name
is on the company letterhead.

143
00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:51.169
- Tom...
- No, no. Come on, we'll just call it a vote.

144
00:06:51.320 --> 00:06:54.164
- Tom...
- Fifty-one percent!

145
00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:55.924
Feels good to win.

146
00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:57.684
You can sell shares at my funeral.

147
00:06:57.760 --> 00:07:00.047
And the next time Ian wants to play CEO,

148
00:07:01.160 --> 00:07:03.401
we can fire him together.

149
00:07:03.880 --> 00:07:05.803
- Hey, can I borrow you for a minute?
- Not now.

150
00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:07.570
It's about the tower.

151
00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:13.967
I already talked to your dad about this.
We're 100 feet taller.

152
00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:15.127
I know that's the projection.

153
00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:16.247
But that's printed to scale.

154
00:07:16.360 --> 00:07:17.691
Chicago's beating us by 60.

155
00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:18.921
Am I missing something here? We're taller.

156
00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:20.690
There's too much steel in their roof.

157
00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:21.841
So?

158
00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:24.685
So that's rated for 760 tons,
and there's nothing on it.

159
00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:26.046
But if they laid that much steel...

160
00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:28.761
They're not done.

161
00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:29.841
No, that's not in their plans.

162
00:07:29.960 --> 00:07:30.961
They know we have their plans.

163
00:07:31.040 --> 00:07:33.401
They want us to think we're winning
but they got a permit for that

164
00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:34.925
and they are beating us by 60 feet.

165
00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:36.365
David!

166
00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:38.209
Right. Keep this quiet.

167
00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:43.691
Oh, Ian, let's make that call
to Madrid before they take their siesta.

168
00:07:43.760 --> 00:07:44.921
Absolutely.

169
00:07:45.640 --> 00:07:47.529
You know, we do have janitors.

170
00:07:47.640 --> 00:07:49.404
- Yeah. I've been busy.
- I got you something.

171
00:07:49.560 --> 00:07:50.561
Ow!

172
00:07:58.640 --> 00:07:59.926
Thanks, Dad.

173
00:08:06.320 --> 00:08:08.926
I'm sorry to break up your dinner,
but I need that report.

174
00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:11.002
Well, tell your wife the check's on me.

175
00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:13.765
Yeah, but she gets another
anniversary next year.

176
00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:15.285
I don't really care.

177
00:08:17.160 --> 00:08:19.242
Oh, excuse me,
have you seen my wife anywhere?

178
00:08:19.320 --> 00:08:20.526
What does she look like?

179
00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:24.844
She is the most beautiful woman
in the entire world.

180
00:08:24.920 --> 00:08:27.048
Oh, well, maybe I have seen her.
Let me see.

181
00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:30.568
Oh, here we go. Is this her?

182
00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:32.851
Oh, let's give her a call.

183
00:08:32.920 --> 00:08:35.366
Yeah, it was a busy day. What did I miss?

184
00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:37.925
Uh, my birthday was last month.

185
00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:39.610
You're joking me right now?

186
00:08:39.800 --> 00:08:41.768
You're gonna have to give me
more to work with than that.

187
00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:46.042
- Oh, damn it. It's not today?
- Tomorrow.

188
00:08:46.120 --> 00:08:47.531
Oh, well, then I haven't missed it.

189
00:08:47.600 --> 00:08:49.045
Father of the year.

190
00:08:49.120 --> 00:08:50.485
So, what did we get her?

191
00:08:50.560 --> 00:08:51.686
Oh, we didn't get her anything.

192
00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:55.725
You were too busy to talk for five minutes,
so I got her a makeup kit.

193
00:08:55.880 --> 00:08:58.929
Oh, well, couldn't we say that
the makeup kit's from both of us?

194
00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:00.923
- No.
- Fine.

195
00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:02.127
What should I get her?

196
00:09:02.760 --> 00:09:05.001
Maybe you should ask her what she wants.

197
00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:06.570
Try getting to know her a little bit

198
00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:08.085
before she heads off to college.

199
00:09:08.240 --> 00:09:10.163
Come on. I still got seven years left.

200
00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:12.288
Or, no, six years. I'm kidding.

201
00:09:12.520 --> 00:09:13.851
Is this how you raised David?

202
00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:15.524
- My son turned out just fine.
- Mmm.

203
00:09:15.600 --> 00:09:17.648
He had to apply for a job to see his dad.

204
00:09:17.720 --> 00:09:19.165
Well, of course.
His mother got full custody.

205
00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:20.241
I had a terrible lawyer.

206
00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:21.731
When you come to Rebecca's party...

207
00:09:21.800 --> 00:09:24.201
Look, we are a month away from opening
the tallest building in...

208
00:09:24.280 --> 00:09:26.931
Tom! When you come to Rebecca's party,

209
00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:29.970
you gotta be here and you have
to bring an exceptional gift.

210
00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:31.161
Daddy!

211
00:09:31.320 --> 00:09:33.448
Hey, baby.

212
00:09:33.640 --> 00:09:36.291
Oh, my goodness.
Those are such fancy pajamas.

213
00:09:36.360 --> 00:09:37.361
Yeah, aren't they?

214
00:09:37.480 --> 00:09:38.925
- They're not pajamas.
- They're not?

215
00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:40.889
But isn't it your bedtime?
What time is her bedtime?

216
00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:42.486
She's coming with us.

217
00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:43.966
Mom says I get to meet the Mayor.

218
00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:45.041
Really?

219
00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:47.363
Quality father-daughter bonding time.

220
00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:49.685
Will there be food?

221
00:09:49.840 --> 00:09:50.921
It's $10,000 a plate.

222
00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:52.001
You're gonna eat like a queen.

223
00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:53.491
Will there be pizza?

224
00:09:53.560 --> 00:09:55.608
Yes, $10,000 pizza.

225
00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:02.370
The children's fund has thrived
under the Mayor's leadership.

226
00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:05.245
And to make sure Mayor Edwards
gets something out of it,

227
00:10:05.320 --> 00:10:07.049
he's gonna lower the voting age to ten.

228
00:10:08.480 --> 00:10:10.801
Everyone asks me why my husband

229
00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:13.048
is hosting a charity event.

230
00:10:13.120 --> 00:10:15.521
The truth is Tom loves children.

231
00:10:15.640 --> 00:10:17.642
He says they make the best smartphones.

232
00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:19.360
I don't get it.

233
00:10:19.400 --> 00:10:20.925
- She just burned your dad.
- Oh.

234
00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:22.764
They say there is no substitute

235
00:10:22.840 --> 00:10:24.444
for time with your children.

236
00:10:24.560 --> 00:10:27.484
Although, we know, in this room,
money comes close.

237
00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:31.926
And that's why this charity is so popular.

238
00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:33.451
If you don't have time for kids,

239
00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:35.045
we'll ease your guilt
by taking your dough.

240
00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:39.961
Which is why Tom Brand has agreed
to host this benefit

241
00:10:40.040 --> 00:10:42.122
for the next seven years.

242
00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:47.010
So without further ado,
please welcome my husband,

243
00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:49.048
a real pussy cat, Tom Brand.

244
00:10:53.520 --> 00:10:55.488
So, today is the big day.

245
00:10:55.560 --> 00:10:56.971
Have you thought about what you want?

246
00:10:57.040 --> 00:10:58.166
I want a cat.

247
00:10:58.240 --> 00:10:59.480
Oh, I don't think our building takes pets.

248
00:10:59.560 --> 00:11:00.721
You own the building.

249
00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:02.211
Wait, didn't you ask for a cat last year?

250
00:11:02.280 --> 00:11:04.169
Yeah, and you got me a foosball table.

251
00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:06.049
Honey, most kids would kill
for a foosball table.

252
00:11:06.120 --> 00:11:07.724
Yeah, but none of my friends
play foosball.

253
00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:09.882
So, at least if I have a cat,
I can play with the cat.

254
00:11:09.960 --> 00:11:11.485
All right, all right.
I'll make you a deal.

255
00:11:11.560 --> 00:11:13.881
- I will think about it. How about that?
- Yes!

256
00:11:16.160 --> 00:11:17.571
Get her jewelry. Girls love jewelry.

257
00:11:17.640 --> 00:11:18.641
Pull some strings with Apple,

258
00:11:18.720 --> 00:11:20.245
get her a prototype of the new iPhone.

259
00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:21.367
How about a private concert?

260
00:11:21.440 --> 00:11:22.930
- You know what band she is into?
- No.

261
00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:24.411
I have a radical suggestion.

262
00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:26.209
Have you tried asking Rebecca
what she wants?

263
00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:28.248
Yes, she wants a cat.

264
00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:29.481
Well, that's in your price range.

265
00:11:29.560 --> 00:11:30.686
I hate cats.

266
00:11:30.760 --> 00:11:32.762
They puke all over the house.
They shed all over everything.

267
00:11:32.840 --> 00:11:34.649
I got an ex-wife, a wife and two kids,

268
00:11:34.720 --> 00:11:35.926
I don't need another thing to feed.

269
00:11:36.120 --> 00:11:37.565
What about a pony?

270
00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:47.643
Could you smile? It's a party.

271
00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:48.881
Why do we always come here?

272
00:11:48.960 --> 00:11:50.769
They're family. More or less.

273
00:11:51.240 --> 00:11:53.846
What are you barking at?
There are no squirrels in the elevator.

274
00:11:55.640 --> 00:11:57.165
Here, take him.

275
00:11:59.960 --> 00:12:01.530
Just pretend you're having fun.

276
00:12:01.640 --> 00:12:03.563
Seriously?

277
00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:09.923
Happy birthday!

278
00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:13.323
I love this yearly ritual

279
00:12:13.400 --> 00:12:15.129
where Tom forgets Rebecca's birthdays

280
00:12:15.200 --> 00:12:17.601
and you forget that Tom
forgets Rebecca's birthdays.

281
00:12:17.680 --> 00:12:18.727
He kind of remembered.

282
00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:21.081
- You'd have to fire a warning shot.
- Madison!

283
00:12:21.160 --> 00:12:23.367
When Tom and I divorced,
he got the younger model.

284
00:12:23.440 --> 00:12:24.566
I'm blushing.

285
00:12:24.680 --> 00:12:26.250
If he loses you, it's jailbait.

286
00:12:26.320 --> 00:12:27.606
Well, that's romantic.

287
00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:30.081
I want you to call my lawyer.

288
00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:31.730
Do you get a finder's fee?

289
00:12:31.800 --> 00:12:33.848
Lara, the day Tom and I divorced

290
00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:35.490
was the happiest day of my life.

291
00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:37.608
I want that happiness for you.

292
00:12:37.680 --> 00:12:39.887
Come on, help me out before
your hands get all shaky.

293
00:12:40.840 --> 00:12:43.969
This is for the road.
I don't want Tom catching us together.

294
00:12:44.040 --> 00:12:46.281
What's he gonna do? Divorce you again?

295
00:12:47.840 --> 00:12:49.365
He would if he could.

296
00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:52.367
Are there gonna be any boys at the party?

297
00:12:52.440 --> 00:12:54.010
No.

298
00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:55.645
You're turning 11, Rebecca.

299
00:12:55.720 --> 00:12:58.451
Now's the time.
I could help you, you know.

300
00:12:58.520 --> 00:13:00.329
Like how my mom helps your mom.

301
00:13:00.400 --> 00:13:02.209
- What?
- Never mind.

302
00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:03.361
I love your room.

303
00:13:03.440 --> 00:13:04.601
Thank you.

304
00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:06.449
My dad actually likes
spending time with me,

305
00:13:06.520 --> 00:13:08.522
so he never has to buy me off.

306
00:13:09.880 --> 00:13:12.565
Come on. Smile for Instagram.

307
00:13:16.240 --> 00:13:17.765
What if you got her a plush cat?

308
00:13:17.840 --> 00:13:19.251
See, technically, it's a cat.

309
00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:20.725
No, technically, it's not a cat.

310
00:13:21.040 --> 00:13:22.485
Chicago just announced.

311
00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:24.802
Hang on. I got it, I got it, I got it.

312
00:13:24.880 --> 00:13:27.281
Take a look at Tashirojima,

313
00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:29.488
also known as Cat Island.

314
00:13:29.560 --> 00:13:30.800
Put her up there with a nanny.

315
00:13:30.880 --> 00:13:32.609
Best part, you don't
even have to be there.

316
00:13:32.680 --> 00:13:33.647
That's interesting.

317
00:13:33.720 --> 00:13:34.926
She asks for a cat every single year.

318
00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:36.166
You can't just buy your way out.

319
00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:38.004
Mr. Brand, I think the fact that

320
00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:39.684
you've had us put so much time
and thought into this

321
00:13:39.760 --> 00:13:41.091
is really gonna show her you care.

322
00:13:41.160 --> 00:13:42.446
If you wanna show her you really care,

323
00:13:42.520 --> 00:13:43.760
just get her what she really wants.

324
00:13:44.080 --> 00:13:45.969
A cat.

325
00:13:47.040 --> 00:13:48.724
Jeez.

326
00:14:05.160 --> 00:14:08.482
Nearest pet shop, 1.7 miles.

327
00:14:15.320 --> 00:14:16.321
Damn it.

328
00:14:16.400 --> 00:14:17.561
Recalculating.

329
00:14:19.400 --> 00:14:23.291
In one-tenth of a mile, make a right turn.

330
00:14:28.920 --> 00:14:30.649
Make a left turn.

331
00:14:37.120 --> 00:14:38.485
You have arrived.

332
00:14:42.520 --> 00:14:43.521
Jeez!

333
00:15:40.640 --> 00:15:42.051
Get away from me.

334
00:15:43.560 --> 00:15:44.561
Shut up.

335
00:15:45.120 --> 00:15:47.646
Hello? Hello?

336
00:15:50.520 --> 00:15:52.249
- Oh, hello.
- Hi.

337
00:15:55.920 --> 00:15:57.809
You look familiar. Have we met?

338
00:15:57.880 --> 00:15:59.041
Oh, I doubt it.

339
00:15:59.120 --> 00:16:00.849
I know you from somewhere.

340
00:16:00.960 --> 00:16:02.689
Well, I'm on TV a lot.

341
00:16:02.760 --> 00:16:05.161
Yes! Animal Planet. I love that show.

342
00:16:05.240 --> 00:16:06.446
No, not Animal Planet.

343
00:16:06.560 --> 00:16:09.530
- I'm Tom Brand. I own FireBrand.
- There you go.

344
00:16:09.600 --> 00:16:12.001
I use newspaper in the poopy boxes,

345
00:16:12.080 --> 00:16:14.481
and I see your face all the time.

346
00:16:15.440 --> 00:16:16.680
Look, I'm a little late for something,

347
00:16:16.760 --> 00:16:18.524
so if we could just get on with it?

348
00:16:18.720 --> 00:16:20.722
- Meow!
- Sure.

349
00:16:20.880 --> 00:16:22.484
You don't like cats, do you, Mr. Brand?

350
00:16:22.560 --> 00:16:24.324
Look, can I just pick one out?
And then I'll be on my way.

351
00:16:24.400 --> 00:16:26.402
You don't pick a cat. The cat picks you.

352
00:16:26.480 --> 00:16:28.164
Look, I make million-dollar
decisions for lunch.

353
00:16:28.240 --> 00:16:29.571
I'm pretty sure I can pick out a cat.

354
00:16:29.640 --> 00:16:31.483
See that? He likes you.

355
00:16:31.560 --> 00:16:34.882
It figures because he's
attracted to troubled souls.

356
00:16:36.920 --> 00:16:38.604
Used up seven lives already.

357
00:16:39.920 --> 00:16:42.048
Meow, meow, meow,
meow, meow, meow, meow, meow

358
00:16:42.120 --> 00:16:44.691
Meow, meow, meow, meow Meow, meow, meow

359
00:16:45.040 --> 00:16:48.249
That'll give Chicago the tallest
building in North America

360
00:16:48.680 --> 00:16:50.603
which leaves New York
and FireBrand in second place.

361
00:16:50.680 --> 00:16:52.364
You should pick a bowl.

362
00:16:52.440 --> 00:16:53.646
The company could not
be reached for comment.

363
00:16:53.720 --> 00:16:55.609
But with the opening ceremony
just a month away...

364
00:16:55.680 --> 00:16:57.409
"Mister Fuzzypants."

365
00:16:57.480 --> 00:17:00.131
Yeah. Yeah. Good.

366
00:17:00.440 --> 00:17:01.680
Good choice.

367
00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:03.571
Yeah. Could you just wrap it up for me?

368
00:17:03.640 --> 00:17:04.687
Sure.

369
00:17:06.280 --> 00:17:07.611
You know, I get it.

370
00:17:07.680 --> 00:17:10.126
"Brand" because your name is Brand.

371
00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:13.882
- But why "Fire"?
- How much do I owe you?

372
00:17:13.960 --> 00:17:16.406
I ask because I did the same thing, see.

373
00:17:16.480 --> 00:17:19.689
My name is Perkins,

374
00:17:19.760 --> 00:17:23.651
so I call my store "Purrkins."

375
00:17:23.720 --> 00:17:26.371
Oh, I see there.

376
00:17:26.920 --> 00:17:29.446
We're just like two peas in a pod.

377
00:17:29.720 --> 00:17:30.926
Yeah. Keep the change.

378
00:17:31.240 --> 00:17:32.526
Oh, wow.

379
00:17:36.720 --> 00:17:39.610
- You might not wanna take that.
- I'm sorry?

380
00:17:39.680 --> 00:17:41.284
You're running late, it's a gift.

381
00:17:41.360 --> 00:17:42.600
You don't want to be late.

382
00:17:45.280 --> 00:17:47.362
For the party?

383
00:17:51.840 --> 00:17:52.841
Right.

384
00:17:54.400 --> 00:17:57.244
Ian, what the hell is going on?

385
00:17:59.560 --> 00:18:01.324
Okay, cats.

386
00:18:01.480 --> 00:18:03.642
Let's do this.

387
00:18:07.880 --> 00:18:09.325
Oh, good job.

388
00:18:10.840 --> 00:18:12.888
- Happy birthday, baby.
- Thank you.

389
00:18:12.960 --> 00:18:14.530
Okay, first piece for the birthday girl.

390
00:18:14.600 --> 00:18:15.965
And save some for Daddy.

391
00:18:16.040 --> 00:18:18.407
Just put it in the freezer
next to last year's slice.

392
00:18:18.520 --> 00:18:20.363
- Mmm.
- What?

393
00:18:26.280 --> 00:18:27.611
Wait here.

394
00:18:51.200 --> 00:18:52.725
Shut up.

395
00:19:03.560 --> 00:19:04.686
Went with the cat.

396
00:19:04.760 --> 00:19:05.807
Smart move.

397
00:19:05.880 --> 00:19:07.291
Was that news report a joke?

398
00:19:07.360 --> 00:19:09.044
Tom, we can turn this around.

399
00:19:09.120 --> 00:19:10.201
Just look up there.

400
00:19:10.280 --> 00:19:11.691
That antenna's 47 feet.

401
00:19:11.760 --> 00:19:12.886
I spoke to our engineers,

402
00:19:12.960 --> 00:19:15.281
and if we install support lines,
we can raise it up.

403
00:19:15.360 --> 00:19:16.441
That's what they did at One World Trade.

404
00:19:16.520 --> 00:19:18.249
Stop. You dragged me across town

405
00:19:18.400 --> 00:19:20.129
and up 1,900 feet to tell me this?

406
00:19:20.200 --> 00:19:21.201
This is a solution.

407
00:19:21.280 --> 00:19:22.770
- That antenna is...
- Antenna?

408
00:19:22.840 --> 00:19:25.366
I wanted the tallest building,
Ian, not the best reception.

409
00:19:25.440 --> 00:19:26.851
Well, maybe we can add more floors.

410
00:19:26.920 --> 00:19:28.331
Do you know how much planning
went into this?

411
00:19:28.400 --> 00:19:29.970
To get permission to build it this height?

412
00:19:30.040 --> 00:19:31.565
You blew it. We're now standing

413
00:19:31.640 --> 00:19:33.130
on the second tallest
building in North America.

414
00:19:33.200 --> 00:19:35.089
Number two, because you were busy

415
00:19:35.160 --> 00:19:37.208
trying to sell my company behind my back.

416
00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:38.651
- Tom...
- Pack up your office!

417
00:19:40.040 --> 00:19:41.610
I'm late. I know. Stop calling.

418
00:19:57.640 --> 00:19:59.210
- Pull me up.
- You're firing me?

419
00:19:59.280 --> 00:20:00.281
Take my hand!

420
00:20:19.280 --> 00:20:20.645
That hurt.

421
00:20:23.000 --> 00:20:24.240
BP holding steady.

422
00:20:24.320 --> 00:20:25.651
Okay, let's do this on three.

423
00:20:25.720 --> 00:20:26.721
Ready?

424
00:20:26.800 --> 00:20:28.802
One, two, three.

425
00:20:32.720 --> 00:20:34.449
What about that guy?

426
00:20:36.640 --> 00:20:38.563
Huh, this little guy looks fine.

427
00:20:41.200 --> 00:20:43.931
Wow, that guy looks worse off than me.

428
00:20:44.000 --> 00:20:46.651
And he's wearing my clothes.

429
00:20:48.160 --> 00:20:50.288
And that's my belt.

430
00:20:55.360 --> 00:20:56.725
Seriously?

431
00:21:00.760 --> 00:21:02.683
It's just a bad dream!

432
00:21:07.400 --> 00:21:08.606
The good news is your husband made it

433
00:21:08.680 --> 00:21:10.409
through surgery with no complications,

434
00:21:10.480 --> 00:21:12.847
but he had severe head trauma
and is unresponsive.

435
00:21:12.920 --> 00:21:14.524
You call this unresponsive?

436
00:21:15.120 --> 00:21:16.246
When will he wake up?

437
00:21:16.320 --> 00:21:17.731
Mrs. Brand, your husband's in a coma.

438
00:21:17.800 --> 00:21:20.963
Once the swelling in the brain is
reduced over the next couple of days,

439
00:21:21.040 --> 00:21:23.008
that's when we're more likely
to see a recovery.

440
00:21:23.080 --> 00:21:24.491
But right now, he's not in there.

441
00:21:24.560 --> 00:21:25.846
That's because I'm in here!

442
00:21:25.920 --> 00:21:27.763
Lara, listen to me! It's me!

443
00:21:30.960 --> 00:21:32.405
Thank God. You can hear me.

444
00:21:34.040 --> 00:21:35.849
Wait, wait, wait, wait.

445
00:21:35.920 --> 00:21:37.001
No, no, no, no.

446
00:21:37.080 --> 00:21:38.809
Don't leave me back there.

447
00:21:38.880 --> 00:21:40.928
Hey, leave me with me.

448
00:21:45.080 --> 00:21:46.127
Hi.

449
00:21:47.720 --> 00:21:48.960
Hi, baby.

450
00:21:49.720 --> 00:21:50.926
Can I see Daddy?

451
00:21:51.000 --> 00:21:54.243
Well, he is sleeping right now
so he can't talk to us,

452
00:21:54.320 --> 00:21:56.084
but maybe he can hear us.

453
00:21:56.160 --> 00:21:57.650
We'll go in together, okay?

454
00:21:57.720 --> 00:21:59.210
- Come on.
- Shall we see?

455
00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:02.048
Oh, this is so humiliating.

456
00:22:02.120 --> 00:22:03.485
Hey, Lara. I tried to lift him up,

457
00:22:03.560 --> 00:22:04.686
but I wasn't strong enough.

458
00:22:04.800 --> 00:22:06.165
- Judas.
- No, it's not your fault.

459
00:22:06.240 --> 00:22:07.480
Whose cat is that?

460
00:22:07.560 --> 00:22:08.846
I think he's yours.

461
00:22:08.920 --> 00:22:10.490
I think your dad got him. Let's go see.

462
00:22:11.000 --> 00:22:13.002
Daddy got me a cat?

463
00:22:13.080 --> 00:22:14.764
Amazing, isn't it?

464
00:22:24.600 --> 00:22:25.647
I said I'd call.

465
00:22:34.600 --> 00:22:36.364
Hello, someone, anyone.

466
00:22:36.440 --> 00:22:38.841
I'm trapped inside a cat's body.

467
00:22:38.960 --> 00:22:40.200
Somebody help me!

468
00:22:40.280 --> 00:22:42.760
You, in the horrible green jacket.

469
00:22:46.000 --> 00:22:49.004
So, how are you doin' in there?

470
00:22:49.080 --> 00:22:51.048
The nightmare continues.

471
00:22:51.120 --> 00:22:53.361
Mr. Brand, this is no dream.

472
00:22:53.440 --> 00:22:54.851
- You can hear me?
- Shh.

473
00:22:54.920 --> 00:22:56.763
I'm a cat whisperer.

474
00:22:56.840 --> 00:22:58.888
And I'm the only one who can hear you.

475
00:22:58.960 --> 00:23:00.121
What did you do to me?

476
00:23:00.200 --> 00:23:02.202
I didn't do anything. You fell off a roof.

477
00:23:02.280 --> 00:23:03.930
Fine. How do I get out of this?

478
00:23:04.000 --> 00:23:05.445
Wrong question.

479
00:23:05.520 --> 00:23:08.000
You should ask, "How did I get into this?"

480
00:23:08.080 --> 00:23:09.684
Fine! How did I get into this?

481
00:23:09.760 --> 00:23:11.330
Keep asking that question.

482
00:23:11.400 --> 00:23:12.890
I hope you figure it out.

483
00:23:12.960 --> 00:23:14.564
What does that mean?

484
00:23:15.080 --> 00:23:16.286
Your body won't last long.

485
00:23:16.360 --> 00:23:19.125
If it expires, you're gonna
be stuck in there

486
00:23:19.200 --> 00:23:20.531
for the rest of your life.

487
00:23:20.600 --> 00:23:22.090
You get me out of here, you son of a...

488
00:23:22.160 --> 00:23:23.491
Calm down, Mr. Brand.

489
00:23:23.560 --> 00:23:25.085
You're a cat.

490
00:23:25.480 --> 00:23:26.891
It's not the end of the world.

491
00:23:26.960 --> 00:23:28.769
I hate cats.

492
00:23:28.840 --> 00:23:30.968
That's what makes this so perfect.

493
00:23:32.680 --> 00:23:34.125
All right.

494
00:23:34.200 --> 00:23:35.929
Calm down.

495
00:23:36.000 --> 00:23:38.651
I thought Daddy would get me a kitten.

496
00:23:38.720 --> 00:23:40.165
He is scruffy, isn't he?

497
00:23:40.840 --> 00:23:42.365
What, you want to trade him in.

498
00:23:42.480 --> 00:23:43.481
No!

499
00:23:43.560 --> 00:23:45.085
I didn't think so.

500
00:23:45.160 --> 00:23:47.242
All right, welcome home, cat.

501
00:23:47.360 --> 00:23:48.361
Oh.

502
00:23:49.400 --> 00:23:51.004
Maybe we should let him get comfortable.

503
00:23:51.080 --> 00:23:53.845
He wants to explore.

504
00:23:54.000 --> 00:23:56.446
Can I sleep with you tonight, Mommy?

505
00:23:57.200 --> 00:23:58.565
Yeah, kiddo.

506
00:23:59.520 --> 00:24:01.284
I could use the company.

507
00:24:01.360 --> 00:24:04.045
Message. Let them know I'm me.

508
00:24:04.120 --> 00:24:05.167
Write a message.

509
00:24:05.240 --> 00:24:06.605
Simple.

510
00:24:06.680 --> 00:24:08.728
"Oh, hi, it's Tom.

511
00:24:08.840 --> 00:24:10.126
"Get me out of here."

512
00:24:10.200 --> 00:24:13.966
Just need a few words.

513
00:24:14.040 --> 00:24:15.530
Nothing complicated.

514
00:24:53.080 --> 00:24:55.526
Dear Lara, don't panic. It's Tom.

515
00:24:55.600 --> 00:24:57.967
I seem to be trapped in the body of a cat.

516
00:24:58.040 --> 00:24:59.201
This is not a joke.

517
00:24:59.280 --> 00:25:01.362
Your loving husband, Tom.

518
00:25:04.480 --> 00:25:06.005
Okay, that didn't work.

519
00:25:06.080 --> 00:25:08.401
Although, not bad for a cat.

520
00:25:21.280 --> 00:25:24.443
Ironically, I could really
use a mouse right now.

521
00:25:30.920 --> 00:25:34.481
Mommy, when is Daddy gonna come home?

522
00:25:34.560 --> 00:25:36.005
Just as soon as he wakes up.

523
00:25:36.120 --> 00:25:38.441
They should use a really big alarm clock.

524
00:25:38.520 --> 00:25:40.443
You'd be a great doctor.

525
00:25:56.920 --> 00:25:57.921
What do you want, kitty?

526
00:25:58.000 --> 00:26:01.561
Money clip, plus license equals...

527
00:26:01.640 --> 00:26:02.880
I'm stuck in a cat!

528
00:26:02.960 --> 00:26:04.325
He wants to play.

529
00:26:06.640 --> 00:26:09.371
Well, sorry, kitty. It is bedtime in here.

530
00:26:09.440 --> 00:26:11.124
But we can play tomorrow.

531
00:26:11.200 --> 00:26:12.281
Tomorrow?

532
00:26:16.000 --> 00:26:17.081
Okay.

533
00:26:22.760 --> 00:26:24.285
Where were we?

534
00:28:18.960 --> 00:28:22.248
If I'm in a cat's body,

535
00:28:22.320 --> 00:28:24.641
is a cat in my body?

536
00:28:26.160 --> 00:28:27.730
Oh...

537
00:28:27.800 --> 00:28:29.962
I always hated that rug.

538
00:28:31.200 --> 00:28:32.201
Whoa!

539
00:28:34.040 --> 00:28:35.804
This is good scotch.

540
00:29:01.400 --> 00:29:02.401
Rough night?

541
00:29:02.480 --> 00:29:04.369
No. I was just contemplating

542
00:29:04.440 --> 00:29:07.125
the rest of my life as a cat.

543
00:29:08.120 --> 00:29:09.121
Hmm.

544
00:29:15.560 --> 00:29:17.289
Okay.

545
00:29:17.400 --> 00:29:19.050
Jesus!

546
00:29:19.240 --> 00:29:20.844
Who's hungry?

547
00:29:27.000 --> 00:29:28.001
Oh...

548
00:29:30.520 --> 00:29:31.521
Yum yum.

549
00:29:37.680 --> 00:29:39.762
Looks like a cat already ate this.

550
00:29:39.880 --> 00:29:41.564
Bon appétit.

551
00:29:41.640 --> 00:29:43.608
French. That'll sell this stuff.

552
00:29:51.880 --> 00:29:53.211
All right.

553
00:29:56.440 --> 00:29:57.646
There's your litter box.

554
00:29:57.720 --> 00:29:59.563
No, thank you, I have the rug.

555
00:30:11.600 --> 00:30:13.648
I had a really good excuse.

556
00:30:15.600 --> 00:30:17.602
Here come the floodgates.

557
00:30:21.400 --> 00:30:23.971
You probably think I'm crazy
crying over a piece of cake.

558
00:30:24.040 --> 00:30:26.520
Or that your husband's
in the hospital in a coma.

559
00:30:26.600 --> 00:30:28.364
He's gonna wake up.

560
00:30:29.280 --> 00:30:30.327
Right?

561
00:30:30.960 --> 00:30:33.281
Oh, I really gotta find that Perkins guy.

562
00:30:36.920 --> 00:30:38.490
Hangover!

563
00:30:40.600 --> 00:30:42.125
Hello, kitty.

564
00:30:42.440 --> 00:30:43.805
What should we call you?

565
00:30:45.320 --> 00:30:47.891
Is that your name? Mister Fuzzypants?

566
00:30:47.960 --> 00:30:49.291
I hate karma.

567
00:30:49.400 --> 00:30:51.926
You're the best gift I ever got.

568
00:30:53.000 --> 00:30:54.445
No, too sweet.

569
00:30:55.560 --> 00:30:57.289
That wasn't funny.

570
00:30:59.120 --> 00:31:00.645
What are you two laughing at?

571
00:31:00.720 --> 00:31:02.882
I don't think it's funny.

572
00:31:02.960 --> 00:31:04.166
See, this is my point of view.

573
00:31:04.240 --> 00:31:07.050
We don't need high rises,
we need strategic growth.

574
00:31:07.120 --> 00:31:08.360
And that's what we've all been saying.

575
00:31:08.440 --> 00:31:10.681
We shouldn't even be
talking about this now.

576
00:31:10.760 --> 00:31:12.000
This isn't a crisis.

577
00:31:12.080 --> 00:31:13.764
This is an opportunity.

578
00:31:31.120 --> 00:31:32.167
What?

579
00:31:36.000 --> 00:31:37.126
What do you need?

580
00:31:50.320 --> 00:31:52.288
If you want food, it's in the bowl.

581
00:31:56.880 --> 00:31:58.041
Fruity Pebbles

582
00:31:59.040 --> 00:32:01.691
or that?

583
00:32:05.040 --> 00:32:06.121
Fruity Pebbles.

584
00:32:13.200 --> 00:32:16.807
Be the cat, be the cat, be the cat,
be the cat, be the cat!

585
00:32:19.400 --> 00:32:20.401
Graceful.

586
00:32:21.520 --> 00:32:22.851
Yeah? You try it.

587
00:32:37.280 --> 00:32:40.329
And, nailed it!

588
00:32:41.120 --> 00:32:42.167
I called your mom, too.

589
00:32:42.240 --> 00:32:43.844
I just wanted to get everyone together.

590
00:32:43.920 --> 00:32:45.126
Well, it smells great.

591
00:32:45.200 --> 00:32:46.850
What are you cooking?

592
00:32:48.480 --> 00:32:50.323
Roast cat.

593
00:32:50.680 --> 00:32:52.728
Maybe its head got screwed up in the fall.

594
00:32:52.800 --> 00:32:54.325
He's an alcoholic. I can't get him to eat,

595
00:32:54.400 --> 00:32:55.640
but I found an empty decanter,

596
00:32:55.720 --> 00:32:57.609
of 50-year-old Macallan
with fur all over it.

597
00:32:57.680 --> 00:32:59.330
Well, at least he has good taste.

598
00:32:59.400 --> 00:33:01.641
Maybe I should mix scotch into his food.

599
00:33:01.720 --> 00:33:02.846
Can I use Dad's office for a bit?

600
00:33:02.920 --> 00:33:03.967
Yeah, what's up?

601
00:33:04.040 --> 00:33:05.690
I just want to see
if I can find anything else

602
00:33:05.760 --> 00:33:07.649
that might help me
with this whole Chicago...

603
00:33:09.480 --> 00:33:11.528
Do they make MRIs for cats?

604
00:33:11.880 --> 00:33:13.405
You mean CAT scans?

605
00:33:14.560 --> 00:33:16.403
I should have landed on the knives.

606
00:33:18.200 --> 00:33:19.611
I'll be in the office.

607
00:33:26.400 --> 00:33:27.731
Hi.

608
00:33:35.040 --> 00:33:36.087
So,

609
00:33:36.200 --> 00:33:37.531
are you like Dad now?

610
00:33:37.960 --> 00:33:39.007
What do you mean?

611
00:33:39.120 --> 00:33:40.531
Are you president of the company?

612
00:33:41.160 --> 00:33:44.050
No, I'm doing the same job,
just without Dad.

613
00:33:44.680 --> 00:33:46.045
Can you come out soon?

614
00:33:46.120 --> 00:33:47.610
Yeah, in a minute.

615
00:33:47.760 --> 00:33:49.922
You're so totally like Dad.

616
00:33:54.040 --> 00:33:55.326
Lara!

617
00:33:55.400 --> 00:33:57.767
Oh, good! Satan's over for dinner.

618
00:33:58.360 --> 00:34:01.364
So sorry about Tom.
I always thought it would be skydiving,

619
00:34:01.440 --> 00:34:02.885
or that his secretary would just snap

620
00:34:02.960 --> 00:34:04.450
and bring an Uzi to the office.

621
00:34:04.600 --> 00:34:06.807
I thought you'd die from a Botox overdose.

622
00:34:07.080 --> 00:34:08.730
Oh, you brought the dogs.

623
00:34:09.840 --> 00:34:11.285
Princess, Jeanette!

624
00:34:21.960 --> 00:34:24.850
You know Tom's unconscious, right?
You can take the night off.

625
00:34:24.920 --> 00:34:26.843
Yeah, well, someone
has to keep things going.

626
00:34:26.960 --> 00:34:29.440
I never understood why you wanted
to work for him anyway.

627
00:34:29.520 --> 00:34:31.363
- Mom, if we could not talk...
- Hey.

628
00:34:31.440 --> 00:34:33.488
This isn't healthy.

629
00:34:51.120 --> 00:34:52.770
Chicken soup for grief.

630
00:34:55.560 --> 00:34:57.005
- Mmm.
- Mmm.

631
00:35:05.440 --> 00:35:06.851
Stop it. Get out of here.

632
00:35:08.680 --> 00:35:09.681
Heel!

633
00:35:11.040 --> 00:35:13.202
Can you please take them away?
They're really scaring him.

634
00:35:13.280 --> 00:35:15.806
They have a very strong sense
about other animals.

635
00:35:15.880 --> 00:35:17.882
- Where'd your dad get him?
- Why?

636
00:35:17.960 --> 00:35:20.008
Well, did he just
pick him up off the streets?

637
00:35:20.080 --> 00:35:21.764
He's just a little messy.

638
00:35:21.880 --> 00:35:24.008
I know you're upset
because your dad's dying...

639
00:35:24.280 --> 00:35:26.886
He's not dying. He's just unconscious.

640
00:35:27.000 --> 00:35:29.890
My mom says your mom should be
more realistic about his condition.

641
00:35:31.640 --> 00:35:33.404
Princess, Jeanette, heel!

642
00:35:35.320 --> 00:35:36.845
T

643
00:35:37.320 --> 00:35:39.163
O

644
00:35:39.560 --> 00:35:40.721
M.

645
00:35:44.200 --> 00:35:45.884
Madison, David, Rebecca, Nicole.

646
00:35:47.120 --> 00:35:48.121
What?

647
00:35:48.400 --> 00:35:49.686
I set a place for Tom.

648
00:35:50.040 --> 00:35:53.249
Well, that's a weird habit.
It's not like he's usually here for dinner.

649
00:35:53.600 --> 00:35:55.045
Madison, not tonight.

650
00:35:55.240 --> 00:35:57.481
I'd say the same thing if he were here.

651
00:35:57.560 --> 00:35:59.005
Yes, that's why nobody likes you.

652
00:35:59.080 --> 00:36:01.162
But there's a reason
you've been seeing Josh.

653
00:36:01.240 --> 00:36:02.287
Josh?

654
00:36:02.360 --> 00:36:04.010
Oh, I can't even think
about that right now.

655
00:36:04.080 --> 00:36:07.163
Now's the perfect time.
It's not like Tom could catch you.

656
00:36:09.960 --> 00:36:11.405
Who needs a litter box?

657
00:36:22.440 --> 00:36:25.683
Oh, Madison? I've been a bad kitty.

658
00:36:27.280 --> 00:36:28.930
Hey! You...

659
00:36:33.000 --> 00:36:34.126
Oh...

660
00:36:34.560 --> 00:36:35.971
Cheese!

661
00:36:48.280 --> 00:36:49.884
Sorry, everybody.

662
00:36:50.800 --> 00:36:51.847
- Wait.
- What?

663
00:36:52.320 --> 00:36:54.800
Nothing, I just thought
I saw... Nothing. It's okay.

664
00:36:55.000 --> 00:36:57.082
Lara, that cat needs to be put down.

665
00:36:57.160 --> 00:36:58.161
Hey!

666
00:36:58.320 --> 00:36:59.560
I'll buy you a new bag, Madison.

667
00:36:59.640 --> 00:37:02.769
Hire a trainer,
a cat whisperer, I don't care.

668
00:37:03.400 --> 00:37:05.164
Let's get you a new martini.

669
00:37:05.520 --> 00:37:06.601
Yes.

670
00:37:06.800 --> 00:37:09.883
Well, someone's gotta talk
about the empty chair.

671
00:37:10.640 --> 00:37:13.041
- Should we do toasts?
- It's not a wake, Mom.

672
00:37:13.360 --> 00:37:15.328
This isn't Tom's
first time in the hospital.

673
00:37:15.640 --> 00:37:17.483
Remember when he launched the airline?

674
00:37:17.560 --> 00:37:19.608
He was always on the phone, never slept.

675
00:37:19.680 --> 00:37:20.920
You know what you asked me?

676
00:37:21.000 --> 00:37:22.047
Vampire.

677
00:37:22.120 --> 00:37:23.770
Why is Daddy a vampire?

678
00:37:24.000 --> 00:37:26.367
Because Mommy sucked all his blood.

679
00:37:26.440 --> 00:37:28.169
He'd stay awake all night working out,

680
00:37:28.240 --> 00:37:30.925
and then one day, he just fell
asleep on a moving treadmill.

681
00:37:31.000 --> 00:37:32.729
He was in the hospital for a week.

682
00:37:33.120 --> 00:37:34.804
Best vacation I ever had.

683
00:37:34.880 --> 00:37:36.848
I'd wake up and find him
on the balcony at 4:00 a.m.

684
00:37:36.920 --> 00:37:38.763
just staring at his tower.

685
00:37:38.840 --> 00:37:39.887
I'll say this for Tom.

686
00:37:39.960 --> 00:37:41.121
There was never another woman.

687
00:37:41.200 --> 00:37:42.361
With me, it was an airline.

688
00:37:42.440 --> 00:37:44.442
With you, it's a big skyscraper.

689
00:37:44.520 --> 00:37:45.931
Ignore everything you hear tonight.

690
00:37:46.120 --> 00:37:47.963
I'm not a role model, Rebecca.

691
00:37:48.040 --> 00:37:49.371
You're used to it.

692
00:37:49.600 --> 00:37:51.204
- How about that toast?
- Mmm-hmm.

693
00:37:51.440 --> 00:37:53.681
- To Dad. Wake up soon.
- We miss you.

694
00:37:53.840 --> 00:37:55.365
Or your tower misses you.

695
00:38:09.880 --> 00:38:11.245
Sleep well?

696
00:38:12.360 --> 00:38:15.762
Rebecca Alison Brand,
your cat destroyed the yellow pages!

697
00:38:15.880 --> 00:38:17.530
What's a yellow pages?

698
00:38:44.480 --> 00:38:45.845
That cat you got,

699
00:38:45.920 --> 00:38:46.887
he's lucky you're in here

700
00:38:46.960 --> 00:38:48.610
or you'd have killed him by now.

701
00:38:48.720 --> 00:38:50.006
I got a plan to beat Chicago.

702
00:38:50.080 --> 00:38:51.923
I just need to sell it to the Board.

703
00:38:52.240 --> 00:38:54.641
When you wake up, we might be number one.

704
00:38:56.000 --> 00:38:57.206
We're doing the best that we can do.

705
00:38:57.280 --> 00:38:58.884
Okay. Thank you so much.

706
00:39:04.680 --> 00:39:05.920
What are you doing here?

707
00:39:06.000 --> 00:39:08.287
Sprained my wrist. That's why
I couldn't hold on to your Dad.

708
00:39:08.360 --> 00:39:10.283
You're seeing my Dad's neurologist
about your wrist?

709
00:39:10.360 --> 00:39:11.521
The Board needs updates on his status.

710
00:39:11.600 --> 00:39:12.761
So ask me.

711
00:39:12.840 --> 00:39:15.161
We're not going to take medical
advice from the grieving son.

712
00:39:15.240 --> 00:39:16.480
It's a massive transition for the company.

713
00:39:16.560 --> 00:39:17.686
What transition?

714
00:39:17.760 --> 00:39:20.206
Big day at the office.
Good luck with the Board.

715
00:39:22.600 --> 00:39:23.886
We're losing by that much.

716
00:39:23.960 --> 00:39:25.405
We get 70 feet, we're number one.

717
00:39:25.480 --> 00:39:27.562
Now, our structure
can't support another floor,

718
00:39:27.640 --> 00:39:31.008
and unfortunately we can't just
smuggle a wrecking ball into Chicago,

719
00:39:31.080 --> 00:39:32.650
so we need to shed weight.

720
00:39:32.720 --> 00:39:33.846
I thought we were making it taller.

721
00:39:34.440 --> 00:39:35.965
We lose one floor,

722
00:39:36.360 --> 00:39:37.566
it buys us this.

723
00:39:37.640 --> 00:39:38.880
That's gonna collapse.

724
00:39:38.960 --> 00:39:40.086
Not if we use titanium.

725
00:39:40.160 --> 00:39:41.366
Why don't we just build it out of gold?

726
00:39:41.480 --> 00:39:43.323
It's as strong as steel
and half the weight.

727
00:39:43.440 --> 00:39:45.761
I don't know what problem
you're trying to solve here.

728
00:39:45.840 --> 00:39:46.841
Excuse me?

729
00:39:46.960 --> 00:39:49.247
This is a stack of prime real
estate in Manhattan.

730
00:39:49.320 --> 00:39:50.731
We can't charge rent on a jungle gym.

731
00:39:50.800 --> 00:39:52.484
My father didn't build
the tallest skyscraper

732
00:39:52.560 --> 00:39:54.688
in the Northern Hemisphere
for a little rent money.

733
00:39:54.760 --> 00:39:56.171
It's not the tallest skyscraper.

734
00:39:56.320 --> 00:39:57.731
Because you screwed up.

735
00:39:57.800 --> 00:39:58.801
Hmm.

736
00:40:01.280 --> 00:40:05.171
Look. If Tom were here, you know
this is exactly what he would do.

737
00:40:05.240 --> 00:40:08.244
I appreciate that you want
to honor your father, David.

738
00:40:08.320 --> 00:40:09.481
We need to watch the books.

739
00:40:09.560 --> 00:40:12.848
Our company can't keep diverting
funds into Tom's pet projects.

740
00:40:13.280 --> 00:40:14.486
It's his company.

741
00:40:14.560 --> 00:40:15.607
Thank you, David.

742
00:40:16.160 --> 00:40:17.685
He's not dead.

743
00:40:30.280 --> 00:40:32.123
- Meow.
- Meow.

744
00:40:32.400 --> 00:40:33.447
You wanna try?

745
00:40:33.520 --> 00:40:34.521
You wanna try?

746
00:40:34.600 --> 00:40:35.840
Lord help me.

747
00:40:36.600 --> 00:40:40.127
Okay, let's try "A purse
is not a litter box."

748
00:40:40.680 --> 00:40:42.603
A purse is not a litter box.

749
00:40:45.920 --> 00:40:48.287
Mr. Fuzzypants was the last thing
her father gave her,

750
00:40:48.360 --> 00:40:49.850
so she's really latched on.

751
00:40:50.040 --> 00:40:52.725
Mmm. He wants attention, obviously.

752
00:40:53.040 --> 00:40:54.883
- This is our daughter, Rebecca.
- Hello.

753
00:40:55.320 --> 00:40:57.049
You are going to tell
them every word I say.

754
00:41:00.160 --> 00:41:01.366
Good move. Nice.

755
00:41:01.640 --> 00:41:02.801
You try it.

756
00:41:02.880 --> 00:41:05.690
Your dad bought this cat at my store.
Did you know that?

757
00:41:05.920 --> 00:41:07.490
Who cares? Just translate.

758
00:41:07.560 --> 00:41:10.723
I remember, he said he wanted you
to have exactly what you asked for.

759
00:41:10.840 --> 00:41:13.684
Hey, cat freak, I didn't call you
down here to ignore me.

760
00:41:14.520 --> 00:41:16.761
Could we have a moment of privacy, please?

761
00:41:18.640 --> 00:41:19.801
You and the cat?

762
00:41:19.880 --> 00:41:20.881
- Yeah.
- Okay.

763
00:41:27.640 --> 00:41:29.881
You don't have time for games, Mr. Brand.

764
00:41:29.960 --> 00:41:31.450
Tell them who I am.

765
00:41:31.520 --> 00:41:33.090
I'm not your press agent.

766
00:41:35.880 --> 00:41:37.006
Well, you're a cat whisperer,

767
00:41:37.080 --> 00:41:39.082
and I'm pretty sure I'm still a cat!

768
00:41:41.920 --> 00:41:43.001
Have you asked yourself

769
00:41:43.080 --> 00:41:44.650
how you got into this position?

770
00:41:44.720 --> 00:41:45.881
I tried googling it, but you know,

771
00:41:45.960 --> 00:41:48.008
they don't make keyboards for paws!

772
00:41:48.080 --> 00:41:51.129
You're acting like a beast
and you're driving your family crazy.

773
00:41:51.200 --> 00:41:53.885
These doctors can't
keep you alive forever,

774
00:41:53.960 --> 00:41:57.601
so if you want to get out of this,
you have to behave.

775
00:41:58.200 --> 00:42:00.931
And if your human body goes,
get used to those paws.

776
00:42:01.000 --> 00:42:02.604
You'll be a cat forever.

777
00:42:06.840 --> 00:42:08.968
I am not eating cat food.

778
00:42:09.240 --> 00:42:10.730
You'll eat cat food or else.

779
00:42:10.840 --> 00:42:12.524
Oh, I'm 10 pounds and covered in fur.

780
00:42:12.600 --> 00:42:14.364
What else could you possibly do to me?

781
00:42:14.440 --> 00:42:16.329
This cat has not been fixed.

782
00:42:16.720 --> 00:42:17.767
Don't you dare.

783
00:42:18.240 --> 00:42:20.368
Oh, should I take him to the vet?

784
00:42:20.440 --> 00:42:21.680
- Perkins...
- Let's wait.

785
00:42:21.760 --> 00:42:23.364
- ...if you so much as lay a finger on...
- He's made progress.

786
00:42:23.440 --> 00:42:25.169
He's gonna be better now.

787
00:42:25.240 --> 00:42:28.130
If he's not eating his food,
using his poopy box,

788
00:42:28.520 --> 00:42:30.807
give me a call. I'll clip him myself.

789
00:42:30.960 --> 00:42:32.121
You hear that, Fuzzypants?

790
00:42:32.200 --> 00:42:34.441
I am the sixth richest
person in Manhattan!

791
00:42:34.520 --> 00:42:35.567
A well-behaved pet

792
00:42:35.640 --> 00:42:37.642
brings love and comfort to a home.

793
00:42:38.320 --> 00:42:41.005
And your family needs that right now,

794
00:42:41.120 --> 00:42:42.201
so are you gonna behave?

795
00:42:42.840 --> 00:42:44.569
You need to be a cat.

796
00:42:45.640 --> 00:42:47.563
Okay, I'll be a cat.

797
00:42:47.640 --> 00:42:48.641
Behave.

798
00:42:50.640 --> 00:42:51.721
No clipping.

799
00:42:53.480 --> 00:42:54.811
All the best.

800
00:42:57.440 --> 00:42:58.521
All the best.

801
00:42:59.920 --> 00:43:01.809
Who needs to be fixed?

802
00:43:02.160 --> 00:43:05.881
Yes, letting salmon breathe
all day really brings out the flavor.

803
00:43:09.120 --> 00:43:11.043
Lord, help me.

804
00:43:12.360 --> 00:43:14.089
How do cats eat this stuff?

805
00:43:16.400 --> 00:43:18.767
Ah... I can't.

806
00:43:21.680 --> 00:43:24.251
I'm starving.

807
00:43:36.560 --> 00:43:40.360
Come on. Come on, Fuzzypants,
you can do it. Come on.

808
00:43:40.960 --> 00:43:42.291
Hold it, hold it still.

809
00:43:42.360 --> 00:43:44.966
Hold it still, hold it, hold it still.

810
00:43:45.200 --> 00:43:46.725
Is this supposed to be fun?

811
00:43:47.960 --> 00:43:48.961
Yeah.

812
00:43:49.720 --> 00:43:51.051
Just drown me.

813
00:43:56.480 --> 00:43:58.289
Well, that's an improvement.

814
00:43:58.880 --> 00:44:00.086
Look.

815
00:44:00.160 --> 00:44:01.321
Seriously?

816
00:44:21.520 --> 00:44:22.567
Good kitty.

817
00:44:23.600 --> 00:44:25.090
Public humiliation.

818
00:44:26.320 --> 00:44:27.321
Hi, Josh.

819
00:44:27.400 --> 00:44:28.447
Josh?

820
00:44:28.560 --> 00:44:30.608
I got something I have to show you.

821
00:44:30.680 --> 00:44:32.250
Look, I can't keep doing this.

822
00:44:32.320 --> 00:44:34.527
No, I'm not taking no for an answer.
I'm already on my way.

823
00:44:34.760 --> 00:44:36.444
Yeah, I'm not gonna...

824
00:44:37.080 --> 00:44:38.525
I'll text you the address, okay?

825
00:44:44.720 --> 00:44:46.245
Don't even think about it.

826
00:44:46.320 --> 00:44:47.845
Come on, get out of there.
I gotta get going.

827
00:44:47.920 --> 00:44:48.921
Let's go.

828
00:45:01.960 --> 00:45:03.450
Missing something?

829
00:45:05.240 --> 00:45:07.368
Here, kitty. Here, kitty.
Here, kitty. Here, kitty.

830
00:45:07.440 --> 00:45:08.487
Kitty, kitty, kitty, kitty.

831
00:45:08.600 --> 00:45:10.011
Oh!

832
00:45:10.360 --> 00:45:11.361
Sorry, honey.

833
00:45:12.120 --> 00:45:14.088
Kitty, kitty. Come on, kitty, kitty.

834
00:45:22.840 --> 00:45:24.126
Of all the cats in the world,

835
00:45:24.240 --> 00:45:26.402
of course Tom picked you.
You're just like him.

836
00:45:26.480 --> 00:45:28.050
That's what I've been trying to tell you.

837
00:45:28.160 --> 00:45:30.766
Stubborn and selfish and shedding.

838
00:45:30.840 --> 00:45:32.205
But here's the difference.

839
00:45:32.280 --> 00:45:34.601
I'm legally barred
from castrating my husband.

840
00:45:35.560 --> 00:45:36.721
Drop 'em.

841
00:45:38.960 --> 00:45:40.007
Good kitty.

842
00:46:17.200 --> 00:46:18.611
Nailed it!

843
00:46:35.320 --> 00:46:36.765
Excuse me, who are you?

844
00:46:38.440 --> 00:46:39.726
Who are you?

845
00:46:40.120 --> 00:46:41.451
None of your business.

846
00:46:45.040 --> 00:46:46.565
We've only got one day in Ohio, so...

847
00:46:46.640 --> 00:46:48.722
- You're selling the company.
- I'll call you back.

848
00:46:48.800 --> 00:46:50.529
You're cutting the books,
you're lining up a roadshow,

849
00:46:50.600 --> 00:46:52.682
and you got Goldman Sachs camped out
in the conference room.

850
00:46:52.760 --> 00:46:53.921
We're taking FireBrand public.

851
00:46:54.160 --> 00:46:56.242
- With the CEO in a coma?
- The odds that he recovers...

852
00:46:56.320 --> 00:46:57.731
- When he wakes up...
- If.

853
00:46:57.840 --> 00:47:01.128
He is gonna fire every single one of you.

854
00:47:01.280 --> 00:47:02.486
Calculated risk.

855
00:47:02.560 --> 00:47:05.131
David, when this deal goes through,
your family makes billions.

856
00:47:05.200 --> 00:47:07.965
Just take the money.
You don't owe Tom Brand a thing.

857
00:47:23.760 --> 00:47:25.125
Hi, Josh.

858
00:47:25.840 --> 00:47:26.841
This is pretty.

859
00:47:27.120 --> 00:47:28.406
It's gorgeous, right?

860
00:47:28.480 --> 00:47:30.403
He's an Abercrombie model?

861
00:47:30.480 --> 00:47:31.720
Wait till you see this view.

862
00:47:37.760 --> 00:47:38.966
- Hi, Josh.
- Hi.

863
00:47:39.840 --> 00:47:41.001
We need to talk.

864
00:47:41.080 --> 00:47:42.127
Let's talk inside.

865
00:47:42.200 --> 00:47:44.282
No, let's just do it out here.

866
00:47:44.400 --> 00:47:45.925
Where, in the grass?

867
00:47:46.000 --> 00:47:47.889
I know that we've been at this for months,

868
00:47:47.960 --> 00:47:50.440
and you must be anxious
for some kind of decision.

869
00:47:50.960 --> 00:47:52.371
I can't keep seeing you.

870
00:47:52.480 --> 00:47:54.482
Lara, just take a look at...

871
00:47:58.000 --> 00:47:59.126
Mr. Fuzzypants?

872
00:47:59.280 --> 00:48:00.281
Seriously?

873
00:48:00.800 --> 00:48:02.802
What are you doing here?

874
00:48:03.080 --> 00:48:05.890
You know, getting out of the city
is really great for a pet.

875
00:48:05.960 --> 00:48:07.405
And this place just went
on the market today.

876
00:48:07.480 --> 00:48:09.528
- Market?
- I can't look at any more houses.

877
00:48:09.600 --> 00:48:10.601
What?

878
00:48:13.640 --> 00:48:14.687
When Madison introduced us,

879
00:48:14.760 --> 00:48:16.091
she said you were ready to buy.

880
00:48:16.160 --> 00:48:17.161
I thought I was.

881
00:48:17.240 --> 00:48:20.483
New house, new job,
I was ready to leave Tom.

882
00:48:20.800 --> 00:48:22.290
She was leaving me.

883
00:48:22.640 --> 00:48:24.642
So, what's changed?

884
00:48:24.720 --> 00:48:27.849
Well, what's changed is
I have this shaggy gremlin,

885
00:48:27.920 --> 00:48:29.604
and even when he's stalking me,

886
00:48:29.680 --> 00:48:33.571
he's a constant reminder, the last thing
Tom did was for his daughter,

887
00:48:33.680 --> 00:48:34.806
and I love him.

888
00:48:34.880 --> 00:48:35.881
And I love you.

889
00:48:35.960 --> 00:48:37.849
- I need to go.
- I never stopped.

890
00:48:41.200 --> 00:48:42.247
Are you happy now?

891
00:48:42.320 --> 00:48:44.049
Not until you are.

892
00:48:47.440 --> 00:48:49.329
- Dr. Cole.
- Uh-oh.

893
00:48:49.840 --> 00:48:51.126
Bad news?

894
00:48:57.560 --> 00:49:01.326
Rebecca, I was just visiting Daddy.

895
00:49:01.840 --> 00:49:03.001
He is still sleeping.

896
00:49:03.080 --> 00:49:05.082
He's getting better, though, right?

897
00:49:05.160 --> 00:49:07.049
His body is getting better,

898
00:49:07.120 --> 00:49:09.202
but he's been sleeping so long,

899
00:49:09.280 --> 00:49:11.806
Dr. Cole doesn't know
if he's gonna wake up.

900
00:49:11.880 --> 00:49:13.370
But he could.

901
00:49:14.000 --> 00:49:15.126
He could.

902
00:49:15.200 --> 00:49:17.362
Mom, then it's gonna be okay.

903
00:49:18.080 --> 00:49:22.244
Dad's been working so hard,
he just needs extra sleep.

904
00:49:29.480 --> 00:49:31.608
Three cool cats

905
00:49:32.960 --> 00:49:35.247
Three cool cats

906
00:49:36.800 --> 00:49:39.929
Parked on the corner in a beat-up car

907
00:49:40.440 --> 00:49:43.569
Dividing up a nickel candy bar

908
00:49:44.720 --> 00:49:47.371
Talking all about how sharp they are

909
00:49:47.440 --> 00:49:49.761
These three cool cats

910
00:49:52.600 --> 00:49:53.840
I'm so sorry, baby.

911
00:49:53.920 --> 00:49:55.081
Not now.

912
00:49:55.800 --> 00:49:58.326
Three cool chicks

913
00:49:59.600 --> 00:50:03.047
Walkin' down the street
Swingin' their hips

914
00:50:03.760 --> 00:50:06.684
Splitting up a bag of potato chips

915
00:50:06.760 --> 00:50:10.606
And three cool cats
did three big flips for

916
00:50:10.920 --> 00:50:13.287
Three cool chicks

917
00:50:14.760 --> 00:50:18.481
Up popped the first cool cat
He said, "Man, look at that!

918
00:50:18.640 --> 00:50:22.087
"Man, do you see what I see?"

919
00:50:22.280 --> 00:50:25.841
- "I want that middle chick!"
- "I want that little chick!"

920
00:50:25.960 --> 00:50:29.009
"Hey, man, save one chick for me!"

921
00:50:29.640 --> 00:50:32.450
Three cool chicks

922
00:50:33.600 --> 00:50:35.443
Three cool chicks

923
00:50:37.040 --> 00:50:40.726
They look like angels from up above

924
00:50:40.880 --> 00:50:44.646
And three cool cats really fell in love

925
00:50:44.760 --> 00:50:48.731
But three cool chicks
made three fools of these

926
00:50:48.800 --> 00:50:50.962
Three cool cats

927
00:50:52.560 --> 00:50:54.403
Three cool cats

928
00:50:54.480 --> 00:50:55.641
What?

929
00:50:56.360 --> 00:50:58.488
Three cool cats

930
00:51:03.600 --> 00:51:05.090
What's wrong?

931
00:51:10.240 --> 00:51:11.480
Oh, boy.

932
00:51:13.000 --> 00:51:14.490
I'm an idiot.

933
00:51:21.480 --> 00:51:23.847
I should have been a better dad.

934
00:51:31.040 --> 00:51:32.087
Hey.

935
00:51:32.160 --> 00:51:33.969
My mom said you needed company right now,

936
00:51:34.040 --> 00:51:36.008
so I'm volunteering my time.

937
00:51:36.080 --> 00:51:37.764
I kind of wanna be alone right now.

938
00:51:39.880 --> 00:51:41.530
You should go wash your face.

939
00:51:41.600 --> 00:51:44.365
Crying really doesn't work
with your complexion.

940
00:51:52.440 --> 00:51:54.010
She's a wreck.

941
00:52:00.880 --> 00:52:01.881
Hey!

942
00:52:10.200 --> 00:52:11.167
Your stupid cat took my...

943
00:52:11.240 --> 00:52:12.969
Why would you share this?

944
00:52:13.040 --> 00:52:14.963
I wanted to show some boys.

945
00:52:15.040 --> 00:52:16.644
If they see you when you're vulnerable,

946
00:52:16.720 --> 00:52:17.801
they'll wanna take care of you and...

947
00:52:17.880 --> 00:52:19.723
You sent this one to half our class.

948
00:52:19.800 --> 00:52:20.847
That was a joke.

949
00:52:20.920 --> 00:52:22.684
You know what, my dad is in the hospital.

950
00:52:22.760 --> 00:52:24.205
Explain the joke to me.

951
00:52:24.280 --> 00:52:25.964
I was just trying to help.

952
00:52:26.080 --> 00:52:27.411
That's what friends do.

953
00:52:27.480 --> 00:52:29.721
You know what,
my mom is friends with your mom,

954
00:52:29.800 --> 00:52:31.290
and I see you over here a lot,

955
00:52:31.360 --> 00:52:32.600
but stop pretending, Nicole.

956
00:52:32.680 --> 00:52:34.250
We're not friends!

957
00:52:41.040 --> 00:52:43.122
I can't believe you just did that!

958
00:52:45.120 --> 00:52:48.488
Good work, but why did you grab her phone?

959
00:52:48.600 --> 00:52:50.090
Because I'm your daddy.

960
00:52:51.080 --> 00:52:52.081
Ew!

961
00:53:01.400 --> 00:53:04.529
Livanto, round and balanced.

962
00:53:04.600 --> 00:53:06.807
I can't play, Mr. Fuzzypants.

963
00:53:11.840 --> 00:53:14.081
That was the right answer.

964
00:53:22.280 --> 00:53:24.567
If this is what it takes to become human,

965
00:53:27.840 --> 00:53:30.730
I will be the best cat that ever lived.

966
00:54:01.000 --> 00:54:04.209
Hey, I brought something
that's gonna wake you up.

967
00:54:04.800 --> 00:54:06.768
An invitation to the grand opening

968
00:54:06.840 --> 00:54:09.320
of the tallest lightning rod

969
00:54:09.400 --> 00:54:11.641
in the Northern Hemisphere.

970
00:54:13.880 --> 00:54:16.486
I miss sharing things with you, Tom.

971
00:54:17.680 --> 00:54:19.728
That's why you need to wake up.

972
00:54:19.800 --> 00:54:23.009
I'm not going to this thing
without a date.

973
00:54:41.680 --> 00:54:43.444
Are you figuring this out?

974
00:54:43.520 --> 00:54:45.170
Hey. I just want
another look at Dad's files.

975
00:54:45.240 --> 00:54:46.287
Okay.

976
00:54:46.360 --> 00:54:48.089
Is everything all right?

977
00:54:50.280 --> 00:54:52.408
They locked up investors this morning.

978
00:54:52.480 --> 00:54:54.528
FireBrand's going to the
New York Stock Exchange.

979
00:54:54.600 --> 00:54:55.681
When?

980
00:54:55.760 --> 00:54:59.446
They're announcing it
when they open the tower.

981
00:54:59.840 --> 00:55:01.490
Ian totally went behind our back.

982
00:55:01.560 --> 00:55:03.562
He's lined up Benson and Stein
and the rest of the Board

983
00:55:03.640 --> 00:55:04.641
in a secret deal.

984
00:55:06.480 --> 00:55:08.323
Turns out, Ian's been working
on this plan for months

985
00:55:08.400 --> 00:55:09.845
and was waiting for the right time.

986
00:55:11.640 --> 00:55:12.766
Tom would kill them.

987
00:55:12.840 --> 00:55:14.444
They don't care.

988
00:55:19.240 --> 00:55:22.210
Did he leave any directives or anything?

989
00:55:22.480 --> 00:55:25.131
Uh, there's a will, but he's not dead.

990
00:55:25.200 --> 00:55:27.089
Yeah, I know, I know. I know.

991
00:55:27.160 --> 00:55:28.730
I just hope there's something in here

992
00:55:28.800 --> 00:55:31.531
that'll help me fight this thing.

993
00:55:39.160 --> 00:55:41.640
Damn. I'm everywhere.

994
00:56:10.640 --> 00:56:12.290
David Brand.

995
00:56:12.720 --> 00:56:14.768
You're gonna need a raise.

996
00:56:20.120 --> 00:56:23.203
But first, let's give you a promotion.

997
00:56:37.640 --> 00:56:40.166
David's pulling files from legal.
He's gonna fight this.

998
00:56:40.240 --> 00:56:41.810
As long as we get to market,
he can't do anything.

999
00:56:49.280 --> 00:56:52.841
Articles of incorporation. Where are they?

1000
00:56:53.680 --> 00:56:55.762
I did find this in Tom's desk.

1001
00:56:55.840 --> 00:56:58.207
He left all his voting shares to David.

1002
00:56:58.480 --> 00:57:00.209
Did the audit find anything like this?

1003
00:57:00.280 --> 00:57:01.281
No.

1004
00:57:01.520 --> 00:57:03.204
David knows. He has to know.

1005
00:57:03.280 --> 00:57:05.248
If he knew, we wouldn't be here.

1006
00:57:05.320 --> 00:57:07.004
I never saw Tom hug David.

1007
00:57:07.080 --> 00:57:08.241
I'm not much of a hugger.

1008
00:57:08.360 --> 00:57:10.601
He's got him working
out of that broom closet.

1009
00:57:10.680 --> 00:57:12.569
I keep wanting to call Child Services.

1010
00:57:12.640 --> 00:57:14.324
Yo!

1011
00:57:14.400 --> 00:57:16.164
Well then,

1012
00:57:16.240 --> 00:57:18.811
I never saw this. Did you?

1013
00:57:18.880 --> 00:57:19.881
Never.

1014
00:57:19.960 --> 00:57:22.964
We all appreciate the way
you've handled this situation.

1015
00:57:23.040 --> 00:57:26.761
If Tom doesn't pull through,
we want you to take the helm.

1016
00:57:26.880 --> 00:57:28.166
- Okay, thank you.
- Hmm.

1017
00:57:31.960 --> 00:57:33.610
- Hang in there.
- Yeah.

1018
00:58:57.200 --> 00:58:58.281
Hey, Mom.

1019
00:58:58.360 --> 00:59:00.328
I hand you the keys
to a multi-billion dollar company

1020
00:59:00.400 --> 00:59:01.401
and you call your mother?

1021
00:59:01.480 --> 00:59:03.369
Do you still have the files
from the divorce?

1022
00:59:03.560 --> 00:59:05.130
Oh, yeah.

1023
00:59:05.200 --> 00:59:07.885
Princess, Jeanette, shut it!

1024
00:59:08.600 --> 00:59:11.888
All of the company records
for the first 10 years are in here.

1025
00:59:11.960 --> 00:59:15.089
Should probably get rid of this stuff,
but it makes me nostalgic.

1026
00:59:15.160 --> 00:59:16.241
- For Dad?
- His money.

1027
00:59:16.320 --> 00:59:17.651
Well, at least you got half.

1028
00:59:18.200 --> 00:59:20.646
I don't know how he did it,
building this company from scratch.

1029
00:59:20.720 --> 00:59:23.530
He never came home. That's how he did it.

1030
00:59:23.600 --> 00:59:24.726
Why are you doing this?

1031
00:59:24.800 --> 00:59:26.529
Are you waiting for
him to say, "Good job"?

1032
00:59:26.600 --> 00:59:28.364
'Cause your father is
never gonna give you that.

1033
00:59:28.480 --> 00:59:30.721
- What's this?
- Well...

1034
00:59:30.800 --> 00:59:31.881
What?

1035
00:59:31.960 --> 00:59:33.041
When your father was just starting off,

1036
00:59:33.120 --> 00:59:34.724
he couldn't think of
a name for the company,

1037
00:59:34.840 --> 00:59:37.241
and then one day,
you drew a picture of him.

1038
00:59:37.320 --> 00:59:39.322
He was never there, but he loved you.

1039
00:59:40.680 --> 00:59:42.091
It's your company, too.

1040
00:59:42.160 --> 00:59:44.162
You named the damn thing.

1041
00:59:44.800 --> 00:59:47.246
It's rare for a company
to be so interested in a patient.

1042
00:59:47.320 --> 00:59:49.004
Tom wasn't just a boss, he was a friend.

1043
00:59:49.080 --> 00:59:50.081
I want to know how he's doing.

1044
00:59:50.160 --> 00:59:52.003
He could wake up tomorrow,
he could stay like this forever.

1045
00:59:52.080 --> 00:59:53.206
We really don't know.

1046
00:59:53.280 --> 00:59:54.884
- Well, what are the odds?
- It's hard to say.

1047
00:59:54.960 --> 00:59:56.485
At this point, less than 1%?

1048
00:59:56.560 --> 00:59:58.528
If you've done your research,
I don't know what else you want.

1049
00:59:58.600 --> 01:00:00.443
I'm concerned that you're
giving his wife false hope.

1050
01:00:00.520 --> 01:00:01.806
I told her we don't know.

1051
01:00:01.880 --> 01:00:04.451
Well, you know, that makes it sound
like it could go either way.

1052
01:00:04.520 --> 01:00:05.487
I can't tell her what to do.

1053
01:00:05.560 --> 01:00:06.971
I just want you to tell her the truth.

1054
01:00:07.080 --> 01:00:09.686
Dragging this out
is so hard on this family.

1055
01:00:10.200 --> 01:00:11.611
Just think about it.

1056
01:00:45.560 --> 01:00:47.801
Lara, you're so beautiful.

1057
01:00:47.880 --> 01:00:49.769
Did I tell you often enough?

1058
01:00:57.160 --> 01:00:58.161
Oh.

1059
01:00:58.240 --> 01:01:01.005
I just wanna say that I'm...

1060
01:01:01.080 --> 01:01:02.047
I'm sorry.

1061
01:01:02.120 --> 01:01:04.088
Hello, there. Come here.

1062
01:01:04.480 --> 01:01:07.131
I'm not in the mood for crazy tonight.

1063
01:01:07.760 --> 01:01:09.000
Good boy.

1064
01:01:12.720 --> 01:01:16.042
I guess this isn't easy for you,
huh, Mr. Fuzzypants?

1065
01:01:16.120 --> 01:01:18.521
Meeting a family like this?

1066
01:01:18.600 --> 01:01:20.204
Do you need a cuddle?

1067
01:01:20.320 --> 01:01:22.129
Somebody need a cuddle tonight?

1068
01:01:28.120 --> 01:01:29.201
Okay.

1069
01:01:29.280 --> 01:01:31.647
This is a special treat just for us.

1070
01:01:32.600 --> 01:01:33.601
Don't tell.

1071
01:01:33.680 --> 01:01:35.967
Sadly, I've got no one to tell.

1072
01:01:41.120 --> 01:01:43.088
How does that feel, huh?

1073
01:01:43.160 --> 01:01:44.730
Very, very sad.

1074
01:01:46.520 --> 01:01:47.965
Good night.

1075
01:01:50.720 --> 01:01:52.131
I love you.

1076
01:01:58.480 --> 01:01:59.641
Lara.

1077
01:02:00.080 --> 01:02:01.605
Lara, wake up.

1078
01:02:08.320 --> 01:02:09.890
Are you trying to be my hairdresser?

1079
01:02:12.880 --> 01:02:13.881
Hello?

1080
01:02:15.560 --> 01:02:17.005
Send him right up.

1081
01:02:21.880 --> 01:02:23.120
Do you have a company to sell?

1082
01:02:23.200 --> 01:02:24.406
No, the tower opening's tonight

1083
01:02:24.480 --> 01:02:25.561
and I didn't see your name on the list.

1084
01:02:25.640 --> 01:02:26.766
I'm not getting out much.

1085
01:02:27.480 --> 01:02:28.481
We'd love to have you.

1086
01:02:28.560 --> 01:02:29.766
I'm sure you would.

1087
01:02:30.160 --> 01:02:32.322
Lara, we all miss Tom very much.

1088
01:02:32.920 --> 01:02:36.686
And maybe it's not my place
to say this, but you have to know.

1089
01:02:36.960 --> 01:02:39.088
- He's not coming back.
- Mom?

1090
01:02:39.320 --> 01:02:40.685
Go back to your room, Rebecca.

1091
01:02:40.760 --> 01:02:42.125
What is he talking about?

1092
01:02:42.200 --> 01:02:44.202
Just get ready for school, okay, sweetie?

1093
01:02:49.360 --> 01:02:50.646
You don't know what you're talking about.

1094
01:02:50.720 --> 01:02:51.960
The doctors say he has a chance.

1095
01:02:52.080 --> 01:02:53.570
I understand. If I were you,

1096
01:02:53.640 --> 01:02:55.847
I would do anything to keep him alive.

1097
01:02:56.400 --> 01:02:58.323
- But this could go on for months.
- I can wait.

1098
01:02:58.400 --> 01:03:00.448
Or years. And he never wakes up.

1099
01:03:00.680 --> 01:03:02.125
And Rebecca, she needs to mourn,

1100
01:03:02.200 --> 01:03:03.486
she can't do that if she's waiting

1101
01:03:03.560 --> 01:03:04.971
for a father who's never coming home.

1102
01:03:05.040 --> 01:03:06.041
Ian, don't...

1103
01:03:09.240 --> 01:03:10.401
- No!
- Oh!

1104
01:03:12.040 --> 01:03:13.769
Get this off of me!

1105
01:03:16.960 --> 01:03:18.928
Please! Get this beast off of me.

1106
01:03:23.200 --> 01:03:24.201
All right, in the cage.

1107
01:03:24.320 --> 01:03:25.321
What did I do?

1108
01:03:25.400 --> 01:03:26.686
You are going into the cage.

1109
01:03:26.760 --> 01:03:29.570
That cat is feral, and you need
to take it to the pound.

1110
01:03:29.640 --> 01:03:30.801
This is a brand new suit!

1111
01:03:33.520 --> 01:03:35.488
He just clawed you before I could.

1112
01:03:35.560 --> 01:03:37.369
- Lara...
- I am not an idiot.

1113
01:03:37.440 --> 01:03:39.044
You're not here because you care about me

1114
01:03:39.120 --> 01:03:40.485
or about Rebecca or about Tom.

1115
01:03:40.560 --> 01:03:43.450
And I am not unplugging my husband
to help your bottom line.

1116
01:03:43.520 --> 01:03:45.488
- Bye, Mom.
- Wait, honey, I'll walk you to school.

1117
01:03:45.560 --> 01:03:48.643
No, it's okay, Mom. It's only
a couple of blocks and I'm 11.

1118
01:03:48.760 --> 01:03:49.886
Okay.

1119
01:03:57.720 --> 01:04:00.769
I understand. You want to protect Rebecca.

1120
01:04:00.840 --> 01:04:03.002
And I want to protect the company.

1121
01:04:03.080 --> 01:04:04.605
But we both need the same thing.

1122
01:04:06.120 --> 01:04:07.121
Goodbye, Ian.

1123
01:04:22.000 --> 01:04:23.411
Where's my dry cleaning?

1124
01:04:23.480 --> 01:04:24.970
Mr. Cox, you're scheduled at the tower.

1125
01:04:25.040 --> 01:04:26.280
Yeah, I know.
Tell the Board I'm running late.

1126
01:04:26.320 --> 01:04:28.448
- Oh, they're in Mr. Brand's office.
- What?

1127
01:04:28.520 --> 01:04:30.602
But I moved up your meeting
with the event planner.

1128
01:04:33.320 --> 01:04:34.481
Why aren't you at the tower?

1129
01:04:34.560 --> 01:04:36.050
- You called a meeting.
- I didn't call a meeting.

1130
01:04:36.120 --> 01:04:37.690
David called the meeting.

1131
01:04:37.760 --> 01:04:38.807
Were you gonna tell me?

1132
01:04:38.880 --> 01:04:40.644
He said he just needed the Board.

1133
01:04:48.960 --> 01:04:50.883
You figured it out.

1134
01:04:59.640 --> 01:05:00.641
Where's the Board?

1135
01:05:00.720 --> 01:05:02.131
I sent them ahead to the tower.

1136
01:05:02.200 --> 01:05:03.281
Sorry they missed your meeting.

1137
01:05:03.360 --> 01:05:04.486
That's okay. We'll do it there.

1138
01:05:04.560 --> 01:05:05.641
We're gonna have a little vote.

1139
01:05:05.720 --> 01:05:07.131
Yeah, you know,
you're not going to the opening.

1140
01:05:07.200 --> 01:05:09.646
- Really?
- Yeah. Mr. Brand no longer works for us.

1141
01:05:09.720 --> 01:05:11.165
He's right. I own the company.

1142
01:05:11.240 --> 01:05:13.129
Not yet. Please escort
him off the property.

1143
01:05:13.200 --> 01:05:14.201
Don't touch me.

1144
01:05:14.280 --> 01:05:16.806
Ian, you do this, I will come
at you with an army of lawyers.

1145
01:05:17.040 --> 01:05:18.326
Go ahead. Sue me.

1146
01:05:18.400 --> 01:05:20.004
Do it tomorrow when we're both rich.

1147
01:05:20.080 --> 01:05:22.560
Do you really think you can steal
FireBrand with a couple of bouncers?

1148
01:05:22.640 --> 01:05:24.449
And you think you can stop me
with a note from Daddy?

1149
01:05:24.520 --> 01:05:26.204
Your father's dying. You lost his company.

1150
01:05:26.280 --> 01:05:28.521
At the end of the day,
you're not Tom Brand.

1151
01:05:51.520 --> 01:05:52.646
Look who's back.

1152
01:05:54.000 --> 01:05:55.729
I knew you'd be back.

1153
01:05:56.760 --> 01:05:58.489
Look who's here.

1154
01:06:07.480 --> 01:06:09.403
What can I do for you, birthday girl?

1155
01:06:09.480 --> 01:06:11.164
I want you to take the cat back.

1156
01:06:11.240 --> 01:06:12.810
What's he done?

1157
01:06:14.360 --> 01:06:16.249
He's been great. It's just...

1158
01:06:16.320 --> 01:06:18.368
I think they might wanna take him away

1159
01:06:18.440 --> 01:06:20.647
and maybe he'd be better off back here.

1160
01:06:20.920 --> 01:06:23.241
I get returns all the time.

1161
01:06:23.520 --> 01:06:26.046
Some cats just don't take
to their new family.

1162
01:06:26.360 --> 01:06:29.250
When I met your father,
I hoped it would work out.

1163
01:06:29.760 --> 01:06:31.922
I know it's stupid, but sometimes I feel

1164
01:06:32.000 --> 01:06:34.241
like my dad's looking out
for me through the cat.

1165
01:06:34.400 --> 01:06:35.526
You miss him.

1166
01:06:35.840 --> 01:06:38.764
I do. I love my dad so much.

1167
01:06:39.000 --> 01:06:40.001
And he loves you,

1168
01:06:40.080 --> 01:06:42.970
but it's not enough
to say you love someone.

1169
01:06:43.040 --> 01:06:44.929
You have to show it. Sometimes,

1170
01:06:46.080 --> 01:06:47.605
love means sacrifice.

1171
01:06:48.520 --> 01:06:49.806
You have to show it.

1172
01:06:52.440 --> 01:06:55.649
When you came to the house,
you were talking to him.

1173
01:06:56.080 --> 01:06:58.287
It's what I do. I'm a cat whisperer.

1174
01:06:59.080 --> 01:07:02.448
Yeah, but you were talking
to him like he was a person.

1175
01:07:04.600 --> 01:07:06.045
Is this cat my dad?

1176
01:07:06.480 --> 01:07:08.403
Perkins, listen. You have to tell her.

1177
01:07:08.680 --> 01:07:10.330
- What do you think?
- Well,

1178
01:07:10.400 --> 01:07:14.610
he makes me feel like my dad's still
around more than he ever was before.

1179
01:07:15.120 --> 01:07:16.121
Sometimes,

1180
01:07:16.760 --> 01:07:19.161
I almost wish my daddy
was more like the cat.

1181
01:07:20.280 --> 01:07:23.090
But I really just want my daddy back.

1182
01:07:24.400 --> 01:07:25.640
Excuse me a minute.

1183
01:07:27.720 --> 01:07:29.722
I'm gonna show you something.

1184
01:07:42.800 --> 01:07:44.484
I'll be right back.

1185
01:07:45.600 --> 01:07:46.601
Wait.

1186
01:07:53.080 --> 01:07:54.127
You should stay with us.

1187
01:07:54.200 --> 01:07:56.009
A cat's life is so much better.

1188
01:07:56.080 --> 01:07:57.684
Thanks, but no thanks.

1189
01:07:58.240 --> 01:08:00.561
We're cold, selfish,
and people still love us.

1190
01:08:00.840 --> 01:08:02.729
That's not who I wanna be.

1191
01:08:02.840 --> 01:08:05.002
Three cool cats

1192
01:08:06.480 --> 01:08:08.847
Three cool cats

1193
01:08:10.080 --> 01:08:11.605
May I have this dance?

1194
01:08:11.680 --> 01:08:13.523
Parked on the corner in a beat-up car

1195
01:08:14.200 --> 01:08:17.443
Dividing up a nickel candy bar

1196
01:08:17.960 --> 01:08:20.964
Talking all about how sharp they are

1197
01:08:21.200 --> 01:08:23.362
These three cool cats

1198
01:08:25.680 --> 01:08:27.967
Three cool chicks

1199
01:08:36.720 --> 01:08:37.801
Clear.

1200
01:08:43.120 --> 01:08:44.645
Rebecca's gonna kill me.

1201
01:08:52.080 --> 01:08:53.127
Hello.

1202
01:08:55.680 --> 01:08:59.526
- "I want that middle chick!"
- "I want that little chick!"

1203
01:08:59.600 --> 01:09:02.251
"Hey, man, save one chick for me!"

1204
01:09:03.280 --> 01:09:05.601
Three cool chicks

1205
01:09:07.080 --> 01:09:09.162
Three cool chicks

1206
01:09:13.080 --> 01:09:14.445
Hey, everything all right?

1207
01:09:14.640 --> 01:09:18.087
And three cool cats really fell in love

1208
01:09:18.160 --> 01:09:22.131
But three cool chicks
made three fools of these

1209
01:09:22.200 --> 01:09:24.771
Three cool cats

1210
01:09:26.080 --> 01:09:33.009
Three cool cats

1211
01:09:37.200 --> 01:09:39.248
You still wanna return the cat?

1212
01:09:40.000 --> 01:09:41.570
No.

1213
01:09:42.000 --> 01:09:44.731
If you want your dad back,
you should get going.

1214
01:09:50.880 --> 01:09:53.770
I think he might be running out of time.

1215
01:09:56.440 --> 01:09:58.602
Dad, when they open the tower tonight...

1216
01:10:12.720 --> 01:10:14.131
Get down.

1217
01:10:15.800 --> 01:10:17.882
We're not seeing
any cerebral activity at all.

1218
01:10:17.960 --> 01:10:20.042
I just don't want to give you false hope.

1219
01:10:20.120 --> 01:10:22.327
There's a possibility
he's not coming back.

1220
01:10:23.480 --> 01:10:25.323
Mom, Dad's still here.

1221
01:10:25.520 --> 01:10:26.646
Can you give us a minute?

1222
01:10:26.720 --> 01:10:28.245
You know how the cat's been acting funny?

1223
01:10:28.320 --> 01:10:29.731
Well, that's because it's Dad.

1224
01:10:29.800 --> 01:10:32.201
- Rebecca...
- Listen, I can prove it.

1225
01:10:32.320 --> 01:10:33.731
Let's talk outside.

1226
01:10:34.720 --> 01:10:35.960
Come on.

1227
01:10:37.840 --> 01:10:39.649
Mom, I'm not making it up.

1228
01:10:40.240 --> 01:10:43.323
Oh, look, I know how you feel.
I miss him, too.

1229
01:10:43.400 --> 01:10:46.609
You'll see, Mommy.
He's really alive in the cat.

1230
01:10:48.680 --> 01:10:50.125
I screwed up, Dad.

1231
01:10:50.320 --> 01:10:51.446
What are you talking about?

1232
01:10:51.920 --> 01:10:55.242
I spent my whole life waiting for
a sign that I was making you proud.

1233
01:10:55.520 --> 01:10:56.931
When I finally got it,

1234
01:10:57.840 --> 01:10:59.171
I let you down.

1235
01:10:59.600 --> 01:11:01.170
I lost everything.

1236
01:11:02.480 --> 01:11:03.686
I can't live with that.

1237
01:11:09.880 --> 01:11:11.530
I don't know if you're still in there,

1238
01:11:12.600 --> 01:11:13.886
but you won't wanna miss this.

1239
01:11:30.240 --> 01:11:32.163
'Cause I'm gonna take my first jump.

1240
01:11:33.880 --> 01:11:36.850
And my last jump right off of that tower.

1241
01:11:36.920 --> 01:11:38.046
No, David!

1242
01:11:39.320 --> 01:11:41.846
Goodbye, Dad. I love you.

1243
01:11:51.040 --> 01:11:52.610
So how does this work?

1244
01:11:53.440 --> 01:11:54.726
You'll need to sign a DNR.

1245
01:11:55.400 --> 01:11:56.401
DNR?

1246
01:11:56.640 --> 01:11:58.290
They're pulling the plug on me?

1247
01:11:58.360 --> 01:12:00.362
And then we'll take out the respirator.

1248
01:12:00.560 --> 01:12:01.561
Daddy.

1249
01:12:01.760 --> 01:12:04.491
Mom, remember how me and Dad
used to dance together?

1250
01:12:04.560 --> 01:12:06.961
- Yeah.
- Just watch, okay? We'll show you, okay?

1251
01:12:07.040 --> 01:12:08.041
Daddy, come here.

1252
01:12:08.480 --> 01:12:10.209
Daddy. Daddy.

1253
01:12:10.400 --> 01:12:12.004
We need to show Mommy our dance.

1254
01:12:12.320 --> 01:12:13.321
Come here.

1255
01:12:14.760 --> 01:12:15.761
Daddy.

1256
01:12:18.000 --> 01:12:19.650
Love means sacrifice.

1257
01:12:20.520 --> 01:12:21.851
Love means sacrifice.

1258
01:12:21.920 --> 01:12:23.649
Daddy! Daddy!

1259
01:12:23.920 --> 01:12:26.446
I'm spending the rest
of my life in a litter box.

1260
01:12:26.920 --> 01:12:27.921
Daddy.

1261
01:12:28.160 --> 01:12:29.161
Daddy!

1262
01:12:29.840 --> 01:12:33.049
Daddy! Daddy, come here!
We have to show her!

1263
01:12:33.680 --> 01:12:36.251
- Daddy! Daddy! What are you doing?
- My baby.

1264
01:12:37.280 --> 01:12:39.328
Oh, honey, I'm sorry.

1265
01:12:42.400 --> 01:12:44.880
Thank you. Isn't she beautiful?

1266
01:12:45.240 --> 01:12:47.720
1,900 feet of glass and steel.

1267
01:12:47.880 --> 01:12:50.724
Now, you can tell
I'm a bit of a numbers guy,

1268
01:12:50.800 --> 01:12:53.121
so, for me, this tower's
more than a legacy.

1269
01:12:53.240 --> 01:12:57.450
Its 2.8 million square feet
of pristine office space.

1270
01:13:09.520 --> 01:13:11.010
Before I even cut a ribbon,

1271
01:13:11.080 --> 01:13:14.801
we've leased 65%
of the tallest building in New York.

1272
01:13:14.880 --> 01:13:16.928
And we're already in negotiations
for the rest of it.

1273
01:13:27.400 --> 01:13:29.004
We can be so much more.

1274
01:13:29.400 --> 01:13:32.449
But this company is greater
than the sum of its parts.

1275
01:13:32.520 --> 01:13:35.046
Beyond real estate, in the last year,

1276
01:13:35.120 --> 01:13:36.963
we've enjoyed record earnings.

1277
01:13:38.040 --> 01:13:39.769
Global retail.

1278
01:13:39.840 --> 01:13:41.729
But before we move on
with our big announcement,

1279
01:13:41.800 --> 01:13:43.962
we have a special guest
who'd like to say a few words.

1280
01:13:44.040 --> 01:13:45.644
Please welcome Mayor Edwards.

1281
01:13:45.720 --> 01:13:46.926
Thank you, Ian.

1282
01:13:49.200 --> 01:13:50.361
New York...

1283
01:13:50.800 --> 01:13:53.007
We're gonna tell Daddy
how much we love him.

1284
01:13:56.320 --> 01:13:57.321
David?

1285
01:14:01.160 --> 01:14:02.321
- I like to take a moment of...
- Hey.

1286
01:14:02.400 --> 01:14:03.765
Wake up in there. Let me in.

1287
01:14:03.840 --> 01:14:05.649
For the dreamer
who made all this possible.

1288
01:14:06.800 --> 01:14:08.040
Tom Brand.

1289
01:14:09.120 --> 01:14:10.884
Now I'm gonna turn this back to Mr. Cox.

1290
01:14:10.960 --> 01:14:13.804
We all wish Tom was here,
but someone's gotta cut the ribbon.

1291
01:14:16.280 --> 01:14:18.169
Oh, come on!

1292
01:14:28.680 --> 01:14:29.681
Wait!

1293
01:14:31.000 --> 01:14:32.684
Thank goodness you found him.

1294
01:14:32.760 --> 01:14:34.046
That thing is yours?

1295
01:14:34.120 --> 01:14:37.249
That's Mr. Fuzzypants. He keeps escaping.

1296
01:14:37.760 --> 01:14:39.569
What kind of name is Fuzzypants?

1297
01:14:39.840 --> 01:14:41.251
Please.

1298
01:14:42.280 --> 01:14:43.281
Thank you.

1299
01:14:45.000 --> 01:14:46.286
You little Houdini.

1300
01:14:46.360 --> 01:14:48.328
He won't bother you anymore. I promise.

1301
01:14:48.400 --> 01:14:49.686
He tried to scratch me.

1302
01:14:50.280 --> 01:14:52.089
That must have been so scary for you.

1303
01:14:52.720 --> 01:14:54.404
Fuzzypants.

1304
01:14:55.040 --> 01:14:56.041
Thank you.

1305
01:15:01.920 --> 01:15:04.844
That was some bold move you
made back there, Mr. Brand.

1306
01:15:05.200 --> 01:15:06.611
Thank you, Perkins.

1307
01:15:09.600 --> 01:15:10.886
If it was me,

1308
01:15:10.960 --> 01:15:12.689
I'd have stayed at the hospital.

1309
01:15:12.760 --> 01:15:14.444
Guess I'm moving into your shop.

1310
01:15:14.520 --> 01:15:15.851
No,

1311
